IMPORT prelude

-- Paid Parental Leave Act 2010 (Cth) -- what a parent can get when a child is born: who may claim and whose permission a
-- partner needs (ss 13(2)(b), (d), (3), 15, 54, 59A); flexible PPL days, how many there are for a child, how many one
-- partnered parent may take and what the PPL rules do to that limit (ss 11D, 31AB(2), (3), 31ABA; PPL rules s 21); days paid
-- to both parents at once (s 21; PPL rules s 7B); eligibility on a day (s 31AA(2), (4); PPL rules s 9); the work test, with
-- paid work for the self-employed, paid leave and the special circumstances (ss 32-36AA; PPL rules ss 22, 23, 24B); the
-- income test (ss 37, 39-41); the Australian residency test and the newly arrived resident's waiting period (ss 31A, 45, 46);
-- when to claim (ss 57A(2), 60); the rate (s 65); who pays -- the employer as paymaster or the Secretary -- and what the
-- employer must do (ss 70-74, 80, 84, 99, 101); and the PPL superannuation contribution (ss 115B, 115C; PPL rules s 36).
--
-- SEAT: the parent -- the birth mother, or her partner or the child's other parent, whether an employee or self-employed --
-- "Am I eligible for parental leave pay, for how many days, at what rate, and who pays me?". Every decision is phrased as
-- the parent asks it. Where the Act addresses the Secretary ("the Secretary must determine ...") it is encoded as what the
-- parent can be paid; where it addresses the employer (ss 72, 74, 80) it is encoded as what the parent must be given. Where
-- the Act hands a judgment to the Secretary (ss 36A, 36AA, 101(4); PPL rules s 7B(5)) it is asked as a fact: "if the
-- Secretary is satisfied that ...".
--
-- Provisions covered: ss 11D, 13(2)(a), (b), (d), (3), 15(1)(a), (3), (4), 21(1), (2), 31A(2)-(4), (7), (7A) (as facts),
-- 31AA(1), (2), (4), 31AB(1)-(3), (8), 31ABA, 32, 33(1), 34(1)(a), (b), (ca), (2), 35(1)-(3), (5), 35A, 36(2), 36A, 36AA, 37,
-- 39, 40, 41(1)(a), (2)(a), 45(1), 46(1), 54(1), 57A(2), 59A(1), (2), 60, 63(3), 65(1), (2), 67(1), 68, 69(1), 70, 71A, 72(1),
-- (1A), 73, 74, 80, 84(2), (2A), 99, 101(1)-(3A), (4) (as a fact), 115B(1), 115C(1), (2), (4), (5). PPL rules ss 7B, 9, 21,
-- 22, 23, 24B, 36.
--
-- Edition: Compilation No. 48, compilation date 1 July 2026 (includes amendments up to Act No. 57, 2025), register id
-- C2026C00294, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/C2010A00104.txt. Paid Parental Leave Rules 2021, Compilation
-- No. 7, compilation date 27 September 2025 (includes amendments up to F2025L01195), register id F2025C00942, as deposited
-- at ../../../paid-parental-leave-rules-2021/registers/source-bundle/F2021L00384.txt.
--
-- NOT ENCODED. Adoption (Part 6-1, the s 13(2)(c), (e), (4) and s 15(1)(b), (c) permissions); exceptional-circumstances and
-- special PPL claims (ss 14, 31AA(5), 31AB(4)-(6), 54(1)(g), (2); PPL rules ss 26-28) -- the day limits here assume that
-- neither the parent nor the partner is in exceptional circumstances; stillbirth and the death of a child or claimant
-- (ss 31AA(3), 31AB(7)); multiple births (s 20); birth verification (s 18); COVID-19 affected claimants and jobkeeper
-- (ss 19B, 33A, 34(1)(e), (f), 35B, 35C); the s 31A(6A), (6B) exemptions and which visas start a waiting period (asked as
-- facts); the s 46(2)-(5) return and extension rules; the indexation of the income limits after 2021 and 2024 (ss 42-44:
-- the indexed amount is an INPUT); "partner", "Australian resident", "income support payment" (Social Security Act
-- meanings) and "adjusted taxable income" (Family Assistance Act Sch 3) -- asked as facts; the national minimum wage (set
-- by a Fair Work Commission order -- an INPUT); the SG charge percentage (Superannuation Guarantee (Administration) Act
-- 1992 s 17A(2) -- an INPUT); instalment periods and paydays (s 64); PPL funding amounts beyond s 73; employer notices,
-- records and responses (ss 81, 82, 102-105); arrears and transfers (ss 85-97); review, debts, compliance and penalties
-- (Chapters 4 and 5); Chapter 3A beyond the amount. Machinery (boards, rule-making power, commencement) is out.
--
-- Dates are written YYYYMMDD as numbers. Adding 10000 gives the same day a year later (a 29 February birthday is not modelled).
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Written straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill, from the seat of the
-- individual to whom the law is applied, with the design defaults ruled on 2026-10-18. No pipeline, no coverage table, no
-- independent test pass, no human gate. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Paid Parental Leave Act 2010`

GIVEN `a` IS A NUMBER
      `b` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the lesser of` MEANS
    IF `a` AT MOST `b` THEN `a` ELSE `b`

GIVEN `a` IS A NUMBER
      `b` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the greater of` MEANS
    IF `a` AT LEAST `b` THEN `a` ELSE `b`

-- INFERENCE, not in the text: the lives count in weeks. The Act counts days; a continuous flexible period is made of "week
-- days" (s 71A; s 6: "week day means a day that is not a Saturday or a Sunday"), so five days to the week is used only to
-- translate.
GIVEN `days` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`in weeks of five week days` MEANS
    `days` DIVIDED BY 5

§§ `s 54 -- who may claim; ss 13(3), 59A -- who needs the birth mother's permission`

-- s 54(1): "Only the following people can make a PPL claim for a child: (a) the child's birth mother; (b) an adoptive parent of
-- the child; (c) a person who: (i) is a parent of the child; and (ii) is not the child's birth mother; (d) the partner of the
-- child's birth mother; (e) the partner of an adoptive parent of the child; (f) the partner of a person covered by paragraph
-- (c); (g) a person who satisfies the circumstances prescribed by the PPL rules as being exceptional circumstances". No
-- paragraph asks whether anyone is married. Gloss: "partner" has the Social Security Act meaning (s 6), asked as a fact.
DECLARE `Who I am to the child` IS ONE OF
    `the birth mother`
    `an adoptive parent`
    `a parent who is not the birth mother`
    `the partner of the birth mother`
    `the partner of an adoptive parent`
    `the partner of a parent who is not the birth mother`
    `someone else caring for the child`

@export May I make a PPL claim for the child (s 54(1))?
GIVEN `who I am` IS A `Who I am to the child` @desc Your relationship to the child
      `I am in exceptional circumstances under the PPL rules` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you satisfy the exceptional circumstances in PPL rules s 26 (asked, not encoded)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I make a PPL claim` IF
    CONSIDER `who I am`
    WHEN `someone else caring for the child` THEN `I am in exceptional circumstances under the PPL rules`
    OTHERWISE TRUE

-- s 59A(1): a PPL claim made by "(a) a person who: (i) is a parent (other than an adoptive parent) of the child; and (ii) is not
-- the child's birth mother; (b) the partner of the child's birth mother; (c) the partner of a person covered by paragraph (a)" is
-- "not an effective claim unless permission to make a claim in relation to the child is given, and has not been revoked, by the
-- child's birth mother". (2): not "in the circumstances prescribed by the PPL rules". The deposited PPL rules contain no
-- provision made for s 59A(2) or s 13(2)(d) (a search of the text for both found none), so the permission is always needed.
-- s 13(3) names the same three people.
@export Do I need the birth mother's permission to claim (ss 13(3), 59A(1))?
GIVEN `who I am` IS A `Who I am to the child` @desc Your relationship to the child
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do I need the birth mother's permission` IF
    CONSIDER `who I am`
    WHEN `a parent who is not the birth mother` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the partner of the birth mother` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the partner of a parent who is not the birth mother` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- s 13(2): the Secretary must determine that parental leave pay is payable if satisfied that "(b) if: (i) the PPL claimant is
-- a person covered by subsection (3); and (ii) the child's birth mother has not previously satisfied the work test in relation
-- to the child; the child's birth mother satisfies the work test on the day the determination is made; ... (d) ... (i) a
-- permission has been given to the PPL claimant under paragraph 15(1)(a) in relation to the child; and (ii) the permission has
-- not been revoked; and (iii) ... the number of flexible PPL days for the child for which parental leave pay would be payable to
-- the person would not exceed the number of flexible PPL days specified in the permission". s 15(3)(b): the permission must
-- "specify the number of flexible PPL days"; s 15(4): the birth mother may vary or revoke it; s 15(6), (7): days already passed
-- are not affected.
@export Does what the birth mother has done let me be paid for these days (s 13(2)(b), (d))?
GIVEN `who I am` IS A `Who I am to the child` @desc Your relationship to the child
      `the birth mother has satisfied the work test` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the birth mother satisfies (or has satisfied) the work test for the child
      `her permission is in force` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the birth mother has given you permission under s 15(1)(a) and not revoked it
      `days in her permission` IS A NUMBER @desc The number of flexible PPL days her permission specifies
      `days I would be paid in all` IS A NUMBER @desc The total days you would be paid for the child if these days were paid
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the birth mother let me be paid for these days` IF
        (NOT (`Do I need the birth mother's permission` `who I am`))
    OR  (    `the birth mother has satisfied the work test`
         AND `her permission is in force`
         AND `days I would be paid in all` AT MOST `days in her permission`)

§§ `s 11D -- flexible PPL days`

-- s 11D: "A day is a flexible PPL day for a child if the day occurs in the period that: (a) starts on the day the child is born;
-- and (b) ends on the day before the child's second birthday." Gloss: a flexible PPL day is a day on which parental leave pay
-- can be paid for the child.
@export Is the day a flexible PPL day for my child (s 11D)?
GIVEN `born on` IS A NUMBER @desc The day your child was born, as YYYYMMDD
      `the day` IS A NUMBER @desc The day you ask about, as YYYYMMDD
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the day a flexible PPL day for my child` IF
        `the day` AT LEAST `born on`
    AND `the day` LESS THAN `born on` PLUS 20000

§§ `ss 31AB(2), (3), 31ABA -- how many days, and the days reserved for the other parent`

-- s 31ABA(1), "Total limit in relation to child": "(a) for a child born before 1 July 2024--100 flexible PPL days ...; (b) ...
-- between 1 July 2024 and 30 June 2025--110 ...; (c) ... between 1 July 2025 and 30 June 2026--120 ...; (d) for a child born on
-- or after 1 July 2026--130 flexible PPL days for the child."
@export How many flexible PPL days can be paid for my child, between everyone (s 31ABA(1))?
GIVEN `born on` IS A NUMBER @desc The day your child was born, as YYYYMMDD
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How many days can be paid for my child` MEANS
    IF `born on` LESS THAN 20240701 THEN 100
    ELSE IF `born on` LESS THAN 20250701 THEN 110
         ELSE IF `born on` LESS THAN 20260701 THEN 120
              ELSE 130

-- s 31ABA(2), "Claimant limit when partnered--reserved period": 90, 100, 105, and "for a child born on or after 1 July 2026--110
-- flexible PPL days for the child". Note 2 to s 31ABA(1): "The difference ... is reserved for other claimants (see section
-- 31AB)."
@export What is the most days I can be paid if I had a partner when I first claimed (s 31ABA(2))?
GIVEN `born on` IS A NUMBER @desc The day your child was born, as YYYYMMDD
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What is the most days I can be paid when partnered` MEANS
    IF `born on` LESS THAN 20240701 THEN 90
    ELSE IF `born on` LESS THAN 20250701 THEN 100
         ELSE IF `born on` LESS THAN 20260701 THEN 105
              ELSE 110

@export How many days are reserved for the other parent (s 31ABA, note 2)?
GIVEN `born on` IS A NUMBER @desc The day your child was born, as YYYYMMDD
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How many days are reserved for the other parent` MEANS
    `How many days can be paid for my child` `born on` MINUS `What is the most days I can be paid when partnered` `born on`

-- PPL rules s 21(1): "For the purposes of paragraph 31AB(3)(d) of the Act, the prescribed conditions are that the relevant
-- claimant satisfies any of subsections (2) to (7)": (2) the partner at the first claim "is incapable of caring for the child"
-- (rules s 7: a parenting order, death, prison, whereabouts unknown, a medical condition, or another reason beyond their
-- control; not a voluntary choice) for "at least 26 weeks"; (3) the child, or a child of the same multiple birth, "is stillborn
-- or has died"; (4) "the relevant claimant is experiencing family and domestic violence, or is dealing with the impacts of
-- family and domestic violence"; (5) the partner "is deployed outside Australia as a defence force member ... for all of the
-- flexible PPL days"; (6), (6A) the child (or a child of the same multiple birth) in hospital, or with higher care needs, "for a
-- period of at least 18 weeks"; (7) the birth mother relinquishing the child (rules s 13).
DECLARE `My circumstances under PPL rules s 21` IS ONE OF
    `none of them`
    `my partner is incapable of caring for the child for at least 26 weeks`
    `the child, or a child of the same birth, is stillborn or has died`
    `I am experiencing family and domestic violence or its impacts`
    `my partner is deployed overseas with the defence force for all the flexible PPL days`
    `the child, or a child of the same birth, is in hospital or has higher care needs for at least 18 weeks`
    `I am the birth mother relinquishing the child as PPL rules s 13 describes`

GIVEN `my circumstances` IS A `My circumstances under PPL rules s 21` @desc Which PPL rules s 21 condition, if any, you satisfy
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do the PPL rules lift my partnered limit` IF
    CONSIDER `my circumstances`
    WHEN `none of them` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

-- s 31AB(2): not eligible once determinations "are in force in relation to the number of flexible PPL days for the child
-- specified in subsection 31ABA(1)" (no exceptional circumstances). (3): not eligible if "(a) the relevant claimant has a partner
-- at the time the relevant claimant makes their first effective claim in relation to the child; and (b) one or more
-- determinations under section 13 that parental leave pay is payable to the relevant claimant are in force in relation to the
-- number of flexible PPL days for the child specified in subsection 31ABA(2)", (c) no exceptional circumstances, and "(d) the
-- relevant claimant does not satisfy the conditions prescribed by the PPL rules for the purposes of this paragraph". Whether a
-- day paid to both parents at once counts once or twice toward the child's total is not said; `days already paid for my child`
-- is asked, which leaves that to the parent.
@export How many more days can I be paid for my child (ss 31AB(2), (3), 31ABA)?
GIVEN `born on` IS A NUMBER @desc The day your child was born, as YYYYMMDD
      `days already paid for my child` IS A NUMBER @desc Days already determined payable for the child, to anyone
      `days already paid to me` IS A NUMBER @desc Days already determined payable to you for the child
      `I had a partner when I first claimed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you had a partner when you made your first effective claim for the child
      `my circumstances` IS A `My circumstances under PPL rules s 21` @desc Which PPL rules s 21 condition, if any, you satisfy
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How many more days can I be paid` MEANS
    IF `I had a partner when I first claimed` AND (NOT (`Do the PPL rules lift my partnered limit` `my circumstances`))
    THEN `the greater of` 0 (`the lesser of`
                                (`How many days can be paid for my child` `born on` MINUS `days already paid for my child`)
                                (`What is the most days I can be paid when partnered` `born on` MINUS `days already paid to me`))
    ELSE `the greater of` 0 (`How many days can be paid for my child` `born on` MINUS `days already paid for my child`)

§§ `s 21 -- days paid to both parents at once`

-- s 21(1): the Secretary "must not make a payability determination that parental leave pay is payable to a person for a flexible
-- PPL day (the relevant day) for a child if: (a) the effect of one or more payability determinations ... is that parental leave
-- pay is payable to more than one person for the same flexible PPL day for the child on a total of: (i) if the child is born
-- before 1 July 2025--10 flexible PPL days; or (ii) if the child is born on or after 1 July 2025--20 flexible PPL days; and (b)
-- ... parental leave pay is payable to another person for the relevant day."
@export How many days can my partner and I both be paid for at once (s 21(1)(a))?
GIVEN `born on` IS A NUMBER @desc The day your child was born, as YYYYMMDD
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How many days can we both be paid for at once` MEANS
    IF `born on` LESS THAN 20250701 THEN 10 ELSE 20

-- s 21(2): "the PPL rules may prescribe circumstances in which a flexible PPL day does not count towards the total". PPL rules
-- s 7B(2): it "would be unreasonable to count the relevant day" because "(a) ... the child's birth mother underwent caesarean
-- delivery ... or ... developed a complication or medical condition in connection with the child's birth; (b) ... the child
-- ... has been or is likely to remain in hospital for a period of at least 14 days; (c) ... the child has higher care needs and
-- requires an extended period of medical care or treatment; (d) on or before the relevant day, the person is affected by a
-- severe medical condition"; (3) the child "is stillborn or has died"; (4) a multiple birth; (5) "the Secretary is satisfied
-- that there is any other reason that makes it unreasonable to count the relevant day".
DECLARE `What happened around the birth` IS ONE OF
    `nothing out of the ordinary`
    `a caesarean delivery, or a complication for the birth mother from the birth`
    `the child in hospital for at least 14 days`
    `the child with higher care needs from a complication or illness`
    `I am affected by a severe medical condition`
    `the child is stillborn or has died`
    `a multiple birth`
    `another reason the Secretary is satisfied makes counting the day unreasonable`

@export Does a day my partner and I are both paid for count toward the limit (s 21(2); PPL rules s 7B)?
GIVEN `what happened` IS A `What happened around the birth` @desc Which PPL rules s 7B circumstance, if any, applies to the day
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does a shared day count toward the limit` IF
    CONSIDER `what happened`
    WHEN `nothing out of the ordinary` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- Read literally, s 21(1) bars the relevant day once the counted total is reached and another person is paid for that day;
-- PPL rules s 7B changes only which days are counted.
@export May I be paid for a day my partner is also paid for (s 21(1))?
GIVEN `born on` IS A NUMBER @desc The day your child was born, as YYYYMMDD
      `shared days already counted` IS A NUMBER @desc Days you and another person have both been determined payable for, leaving out days that do not count
      `someone else is paid for the day` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether parental leave pay is payable to another person for the day you ask about
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I be paid for a shared day` IF
    (NOT (    `shared days already counted` AT LEAST `How many days can we both be paid for at once` `born on`
          AND `someone else is paid for the day`))

§§ `s 31AA -- am I eligible on the day`

-- s 31AA(1): eligible on a flexible PPL day if eligible "under subsection (2), (3), (4) or (5)" and "not ineligible ... under
-- section 31AB". (2), the main rule: "(a) the person satisfies the Australian residency test on that day; and (b) the person is
-- caring for the child on that day; and (c) on that day the person is performing no more than one hour of paid work; and (d) if
-- the person has not previously satisfied the work and income tests in relation to the child--the person satisfies the work
-- test and the income test on that day; and (e) ... (i) the person satisfies the Australian residency test on the day the child
-- was born; (ii) if the day the child was born is in a newly arrived resident's waiting period ... subsection 31A(7) or (7A)
-- applies to the person on the day the child was born."
-- (4), the PPL rules route, has the same residency, work and income test and birth-day conditions, and instead of (b) and (c)
-- "(e) on that flexible PPL day, the person satisfies the conditions prescribed by the PPL rules". PPL rules s 9(2): "is caring
-- for the child on that day" or satisfies rules s 13 (birth mother relinquishing), s 16 (temporary inability to care) or s 17
-- (loss of care); s 9(3): "is performing no more than one hour of paid work on that day" or satisfies rules s 13 (because of
-- 13(2)(b)), s 14 (child in hospital following birth), s 17, s 18 (recall to duty), s 19 (summons) or s 20 (emergency).
-- s 31AA(4)(d) (not in special-PPL exceptional circumstances) is assumed.
-- s 31AB(8): ineligible on a day "in a newly arrived resident's waiting period", unless s 31A(7) or (7A) applies that day (s 31A(7),
-- (7A): a holder of a determined visa class, a refugee or former refugee or their family member, an Australian citizen, or a
-- special category visa holder residing in Australia).
-- `married to the child's other parent` is on the record and used by no rule: nothing in Part 2-3 asks.
DECLARE `Me on the day` HAS
    `I satisfy the Australian residency test on the day` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I satisfied it on the day my child was born` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I am caring for my child on the day` IS A BOOLEAN
    `hours of paid work I do on the day` IS A NUMBER
    `I have previously satisfied the work and income tests for my child` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I satisfy the work test` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I satisfy the income test` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the day my child was born is in my waiting period` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 31A(7) or (7A) applied to me on the day my child was born` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the day is in my waiting period` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 31A(7) or (7A) applies to me on the day` IS A BOOLEAN
    `PPL rules s 13, 16 or 17 explains my not caring for my child` IS A BOOLEAN
    `PPL rules s 13, 14, 17, 18, 19 or 20 explains my paid work` IS A BOOLEAN
    `married to the child's other parent` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `me` IS A `Me on the day` @desc Your circumstances on the day
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the conditions common to s 31AA(2) and (4) are met` IF
        `me`'s `I satisfy the Australian residency test on the day`
    AND (    `me`'s `I have previously satisfied the work and income tests for my child`
         OR  (`me`'s `I satisfy the work test` AND `me`'s `I satisfy the income test`))
    AND `me`'s `I satisfied it on the day my child was born`
    AND (    (NOT (`me`'s `the day my child was born is in my waiting period`))
         OR  `me`'s `s 31A(7) or (7A) applied to me on the day my child was born`)

GIVEN `me` IS A `Me on the day` @desc Your circumstances on the day
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the main rule in s 31AA(2) is met` IF
        `the conditions common to s 31AA(2) and (4) are met` `me`
    AND `me`'s `I am caring for my child on the day`
    AND `me`'s `hours of paid work I do on the day` AT MOST 1

GIVEN `me` IS A `Me on the day` @desc Your circumstances on the day
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the PPL rules route in s 31AA(4) is met` IF
        `the conditions common to s 31AA(2) and (4) are met` `me`
    AND (`me`'s `I am caring for my child on the day` OR `me`'s `PPL rules s 13, 16 or 17 explains my not caring for my child`)
    AND (`me`'s `hours of paid work I do on the day` AT MOST 1 OR `me`'s `PPL rules s 13, 14, 17, 18, 19 or 20 explains my paid work`)

@export Am I eligible for parental leave pay on the day (ss 31AA, 31AB)?
GIVEN `me` IS A `Me on the day` @desc Your circumstances on the day
      `more days I can be paid` IS A NUMBER @desc The answer to "How many more days can I be paid for my child"
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I eligible on the day` IF
        (`the main rule in s 31AA(2) is met` `me` OR `the PPL rules route in s 31AA(4) is met` `me`)
    AND `more days I can be paid` GREATER THAN 0
    AND (    (NOT (`me`'s `the day is in my waiting period`))
         OR  `me`'s `s 31A(7) or (7A) applies to me on the day`)

§§ `ss 32, 33, 36, 36A, 36AA -- the work test`

-- s 32, Step 4: "a period (a qualifying period) of 295 consecutive days in the work test period that are days: (a) on which the
-- person has performed qualifying work; or (b) that fall within a permissible break"; Step 5: "If the person has performed at
-- least 330 hours of qualifying work in a qualifying period, the person satisfies the work test."
-- s 36A(1): "also satisfies the work test" if "the Secretary is satisfied" that "(i) if the person is covered by subsection
-- (2)--the child was born prematurely; (ii) if the person is the child's birth mother--while the person was pregnant with the
-- child, the person had complications or illness related to the pregnancy which prevented the person from performing paid work"
-- and that the person "would have satisfied the work test ... if that circumstance ... had not existed". (2) covers the birth
-- mother, a parent who is not the birth mother, and the partner of the birth mother.
-- s 36AA: the same, for "special circumstances of a kind prescribed by the PPL rules". PPL rules s 24B(2): "(a) the person is
-- experiencing family and domestic violence, or is dealing with the impact of family and domestic violence, that prevents the
-- person from performing paid work; or (b) the person is affected by a severe medical condition that prevents the person from
-- performing paid work; or (c) the person is caring for a family member who is affected by a severe medical condition and
-- providing such care prevents the person from performing paid work; or (d) the person is severely affected by a natural
-- disaster that: (i) has been declared ...; and (ii) prevents the person from performing paid work."
DECLARE `What kept me from working` IS ONE OF
    `nothing`
    `my child was born prematurely`
    `complications or illness in my pregnancy`
    `family and domestic violence`
    `a severe medical condition of mine`
    `caring for a family member with a severe medical condition`
    `a declared natural disaster`

DECLARE `My work history` HAS
    `longest run of qualifying work days and permissible breaks in my work test period` IS A NUMBER
    `hours of qualifying work in that run` IS A NUMBER
    `what kept me from working` IS A `What kept me from working`
    `the Secretary is satisfied I would otherwise have satisfied the work test` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `who I am` IS A `Who I am to the child` @desc Your relationship to the child
      `what kept me` IS A `What kept me from working` @desc What, if anything, kept you from working
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the circumstance is one ss 36A and 36AA recognise for me` IF
    CONSIDER `what kept me`
    WHEN `nothing` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `my child was born prematurely` THEN
        CONSIDER `who I am`
        WHEN `the birth mother` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `a parent who is not the birth mother` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `the partner of the birth mother` THEN TRUE
        OTHERWISE FALSE
    WHEN `complications or illness in my pregnancy` THEN
        CONSIDER `who I am`
        WHEN `the birth mother` THEN TRUE
        OTHERWISE FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

@export Do I satisfy the work test (ss 32, 36A, 36AA)?
GIVEN `who I am` IS A `Who I am to the child` @desc Your relationship to the child
      `history` IS A `My work history` @desc Your work in the work test period
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do I satisfy the work test` IF
        (    `history`'s `longest run of qualifying work days and permissible breaks in my work test period` AT LEAST 295
         AND `history`'s `hours of qualifying work in that run` AT LEAST 330)
    OR  (    `the circumstance is one ss 36A and 36AA recognise for me` `who I am` (`history`'s `what kept me from working`)
         AND `history`'s `the Secretary is satisfied I would otherwise have satisfied the work test`)

-- s 33(1): "The work test period ... is the 392 days immediately before: (a) if: (i) subsection (2A) applies ...; and (ii) [the
-- claimant] would not satisfy the work test if the claimant's work test period were the work test period under paragraph (b) or
-- (c) ...; the claimant's work cessation day; or (b) if: (i) the child ... is born after the expected date of birth of the child;
-- and (ii) [the claimant] would not satisfy the work test if the claimant's work test period were the work test period under
-- paragraph (c) ...; the expected date of birth of the child; or (c) otherwise--the day the child is born." (2A): the pregnant
-- claimant or birth mother stopped "because of hazards connected with that kind of work that pose or posed a risk to the
-- pregnancy". (The 600-day period of s 33A is for COVID-19 affected claimants, whom s 19B bars for a child born after 31 March
-- 2021.)
DECLARE `The day my work test period runs back from` IS ONE OF
    `my work cessation day`
    `the expected date of birth`
    `the day my child was born`

@export Which day does my 392-day work test period run back from (s 33(1))?
GIVEN `I stopped hazardous work as s 33(2A) describes and fail the test otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether s 33(2A) applies and you would fail the test under paras (b) and (c)
      `my child was born late and I fail the test otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your child was born after the expected date and you would fail the test counting back from the birth
GIVETH A `The day my work test period runs back from`
`Which day does my work test period run back from` MEANS
    IF `I stopped hazardous work as s 33(2A) describes and fail the test otherwise` THEN `my work cessation day`
    ELSE IF `my child was born late and I fail the test otherwise` THEN `the expected date of birth`
         ELSE `the day my child was born`

-- s 36(2): "at least 1 day but not more than 84 consecutive days on which the person did not perform qualifying work" between two
-- qualifying work days "is a permissible break". Gloss: a gap that does not break the run.
@export Is a gap between two days of qualifying work a permissible break (s 36(2))?
GIVEN `days without qualifying work` IS A NUMBER @desc The number of consecutive days in the gap
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the gap a permissible break` IF
        `days without qualifying work` AT LEAST 1
    AND `days without qualifying work` AT MOST 84

§§ `ss 34, 35, 35A -- qualifying work, paid work and the self-employed`

-- s 35(1): paid work is work "(whether as an employee, a contractor or otherwise and whether or not in Australia) for another
-- entity for remuneration or other financial benefit"; (2): "However, a person is taken not to perform paid work for the purposes
-- of subsection (1) if the other entity is controlled by the person"; (3), "Self-employed": "A person performs paid work on a day
-- if, on that day, the person performs work for the purposes of a business that is carried on for profit ... by: (a) the person
-- (whether alone or with others); or (b) an entity that is controlled by the person". (5): the PPL rules "may prescribe what is,
-- or is not, taken to be paid work". PPL rules s 23(1): not paid work -- "(a) an activity required ... as a condition for the
-- person receiving a social security payment"; "(b) work performed by a person who is a prisoner (other than ... a formal
-- prisoner employment program)"; "(c) an activity engaged in by a person as a volunteer"; "(d) the receipt of ... interest;
-- ... rents, dividends ...; ... any other income that is not obtained as a result of ... the personal exertion of the person"
-- (subject to s 23(2) for money lenders and trade debts -- not modelled).
DECLARE `My activity on the day` HAS
    `I work for another entity for pay` IS A BOOLEAN
    `that entity is controlled by me` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I work for a business carried on for profit by me or an entity I control` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the activity is one PPL rules s 23 says is not paid work` IS A BOOLEAN

@export Do I perform paid work on the day (s 35; PPL rules s 23)?
GIVEN `activity` IS A `My activity on the day` @desc What you did on the day
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do I perform paid work` IF
        (NOT (`activity`'s `the activity is one PPL rules s 23 says is not paid work`))
    AND (    (`activity`'s `I work for another entity for pay` AND (NOT (`activity`'s `that entity is controlled by me`)))
         OR  `activity`'s `I work for a business carried on for profit by me or an entity I control`)

-- s 34(1): qualifying work on a day if "(a) the person performs at least one hour of paid work; (b) the person takes a period of
-- paid leave of at least one hour; (ca) the day is a flexible PPL day for a previous child of the person and parental leave pay
-- was payable to the person on that day". (2): the PPL rules may say what is paid leave. PPL rules s 22: "unpaid leave taken by
-- a person on a day is taken to be paid leave" if the person "receives a payment for workers' compensation or accident
-- compensation for that day", relating to their employment, "from an entity other than the employer".
@export Is the day a day of qualifying work for me (s 34; PPL rules s 22)?
GIVEN `hours of paid work` IS A NUMBER @desc Hours of paid work you did on the day
      `hours of paid leave` IS A NUMBER @desc Hours of paid leave you took on the day
      `hours of unpaid leave with compensation from someone other than my employer` IS A NUMBER @desc Hours of unpaid leave on a day you were paid workers' or accident compensation by an entity other than your employer
      `I was paid parental leave pay for a previous child that day` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the day was a paid flexible PPL day for an earlier child of yours
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the day a qualifying work day` IF
        `hours of paid work` AT LEAST 1
    OR  `hours of paid leave` PLUS `hours of unpaid leave with compensation from someone other than my employer` AT LEAST 1
    OR  `I was paid parental leave pay for a previous child that day`

-- s 35A(1): on a day that is qualifying work "only because the day is a flexible PPL day for a previous child, the person is
-- taken to have performed 7.6 hours of work"; (2), (3): if the person also worked or took paid leave, "the greater of" 7.6 and
-- those hours.
@export How many hours of qualifying work does a paid PPL day for an earlier child count for (s 35A)?
GIVEN `hours of paid work or paid leave that day` IS A NUMBER @desc Hours of paid work or paid leave you also had on that day
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How many hours does a PPL day for an earlier child count for` MEANS
    `the greater of` 7.6 `hours of paid work or paid leave that day`

§§ `ss 37, 39, 40, 41 -- the income test`

-- s 37: satisfied if "(1) ... the person's adjusted taxable income for the reference income year is not more than the relevant
-- individual PPL income limit"; or "(2) ... (c) the person does not have a partner at the time the person makes the claim ... and
-- (d) the person's adjusted taxable income ... is not more than the relevant family PPL income limit"; or "(3) ... (c) the person
-- has a partner ... and (d) the total of ... the person's adjusted taxable income ... [and] the adjusted taxable income of the
-- person's partner ... is not more than the relevant family PPL income limit". The three are alternatives.
@export Do I satisfy the income test (s 37)?
GIVEN `my adjusted taxable income` IS A NUMBER @desc Your adjusted taxable income for the reference income year
      `I have a partner when I claim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have a partner when you make the claim
      `my partner's adjusted taxable income` IS A NUMBER @desc Your partner's adjusted taxable income for the reference income year
      `the individual limit` IS A NUMBER @desc The relevant individual PPL income limit (s 40)
      `the family limit` IS A NUMBER @desc The relevant family PPL income limit (s 40)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do I satisfy the income test` IF
        `my adjusted taxable income` AT MOST `the individual limit`
    OR  ((NOT `I have a partner when I claim`) AND `my adjusted taxable income` AT MOST `the family limit`)
    OR  (`I have a partner when I claim` AND `my adjusted taxable income` PLUS `my partner's adjusted taxable income` AT MOST `the family limit`)

-- s 39: "The reference income year for a person is: (a) the income year that ended before the earlier of: (i) the day the person
-- made the claim; and (ii) the day the child was born." s 40: the relevant limits are those that apply on the same earlier day.
-- Gloss: an income year runs from 1 July to 30 June; the answer is the calendar year in which it ended.
GIVEN `the day` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the calendar year of` MEANS TRUNC (`the day` DIVIDED BY 10000) 0

@export My reference income year is the one that ended on 30 June of which year (s 39)?
GIVEN `claimed on` IS A NUMBER @desc The day you made the claim, as YYYYMMDD
      `born on` IS A NUMBER @desc The day your child was born, as YYYYMMDD
GIVETH A NUMBER
`My reference income year ended on 30 June of` MEANS
    IF `the earlier day` MINUS `the calendar year of` `the earlier day` TIMES 10000 AT LEAST 701
    THEN `the calendar year of` `the earlier day`
    ELSE `the calendar year of` `the earlier day` MINUS 1
    WHERE
        `the earlier day` MEANS `the lesser of` `claimed on` `born on`

-- s 41(1): the individual PPL income limit is "(a) if the day is on or after 1 October 2010 but before 1 July 2021--$150,000";
-- then the indexed amount (ss 42-44, CPI -- an INPUT). (2): the family PPL income limit is "(a) if the day is on or after 1 July
-- 2023 but before 1 July 2024--$350,000"; then indexed from 1 July 2024 (an INPUT).
@export What is the individual PPL income limit on the day (s 41(1))?
GIVEN `the day` IS A NUMBER @desc The earlier of your claim day and your child's birth, as YYYYMMDD
      `the indexed amount in force` IS A NUMBER @desc The indexed limit in force that day, if after 30 June 2021
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What is the individual PPL income limit` MEANS
    IF `the day` AT LEAST 20101001 AND `the day` LESS THAN 20210701 THEN 150000 ELSE `the indexed amount in force`

@export What is the family PPL income limit on the day (s 41(2))?
GIVEN `the day` IS A NUMBER @desc The earlier of your claim day and your child's birth, as YYYYMMDD
      `the indexed amount in force` IS A NUMBER @desc The indexed limit in force that day, if after 30 June 2024
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What is the family PPL income limit` MEANS
    IF `the day` AT LEAST 20230701 AND `the day` LESS THAN 20240701 THEN 350000 ELSE `the indexed amount in force`

§§ `ss 31A, 45, 46 -- residency and the waiting period`

-- s 45(1): satisfied on a day if the person "(a) is an Australian resident; or (b) is a special category visa holder residing in
-- Australia; or (c) satisfies subsection (2)" (a holder of a visa determined under the Social Security Act who is in Australia or
-- briefly and allowably absent). s 46(1): "Despite section 45, a person does not satisfy the Australian residency test ... if ...
-- the person has been absent from Australia for more than 56 weeks since the day the person left Australia" (the return and
-- extension rules in (2)-(5) are not modelled).
@export Do I satisfy the Australian residency test on the day (ss 45, 46)?
GIVEN `I am an Australian resident` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are an Australian resident (Social Security Act meaning)
      `I am a special category visa holder residing in Australia` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you hold a special category visa and reside in Australia
      `I satisfy s 45(2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you hold a visa determined under SSA s 729(2)(f)(v) and are in Australia (or allowably absent 6 weeks or less)
      `weeks I have been absent from Australia` IS A NUMBER @desc Weeks since you last left Australia, if you are away (0 if not)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do I satisfy the Australian residency test` IF
        (`I am an Australian resident` OR `I am a special category visa holder residing in Australia` OR `I satisfy s 45(2)`)
    AND `weeks I have been absent from Australia` AT MOST 56

-- s 31A(1)(b): a person who "becomes the holder of a permanent visa" (with exceptions) is "subject to a newly arrived resident's
-- waiting period". (2)-(4): it ends "when the person has been in Australia for a period of, or periods totalling, 104 weeks"
-- after its start. Which start applies depends on visa classes determined under the Social Security Act (asked as a fact).
@export Has my newly arrived resident's waiting period ended (s 31A(2)-(4))?
GIVEN `days in Australia since my waiting period began` IS A NUMBER @desc Days you have been in Australia, in total, since the waiting period started
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Has my waiting period ended` IF
    `days in Australia since my waiting period began` AT LEAST 104 TIMES 7

§§ `ss 57A(2), 60 -- when to claim`

-- s 60: a claim "must be made in the period that: (a) starts on the day that is 97 days before the expected date of birth of the
-- child; and (b) ends on the day before: (i) if, before the child's first birthday, an effective claim for parental leave pay for
-- the child has been made by a PPL claimant for the child--the child's second birthday; or (ii) otherwise--the child's first
-- birthday."
@export Am I in time to claim (s 60)?
GIVEN `days before the expected date of birth that I claim` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days before the expected date of birth you claim (negative if after)
      `my child's age in completed years` IS A NUMBER @desc Your child's age in whole years when you claim (0 if not yet born)
      `someone claimed for my child before the first birthday` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether an effective PPL claim for the child was made before the first birthday
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I in time to claim` IF
        `days before the expected date of birth that I claim` AT MOST 97
    AND (    `my child's age in completed years` LESS THAN 1
         OR  (`someone claimed for my child before the first birthday` AND `my child's age in completed years` LESS THAN 2))

-- s 57A(2): "A flexible PPL day for the child specified in the claim must not be a day that is more than 100 days before the day
-- the claim is made." Gloss: a claim can reach back at most 100 days.
@export Can my claim include a day this many days before I claim (s 57A(2))?
GIVEN `days before my claim` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days before the claim day the flexible PPL day falls
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can my claim reach back to the day` IF
    `days before my claim` AT MOST 100

§§ `ss 63, 65 -- how much I am paid`

-- s 65(2): "The daily national minimum wage amount for a day is 7.6 times the amount of the national minimum wage (when expressed
-- as a monetary amount per hour) set by a national minimum wage order that is in operation on that day". (1): an instalment is
-- "the sum of the daily national minimum wage amounts for each day, during the instalment period ..., that is: (a) a flexible PPL
-- day for a child of the person; and (b) a day for which parental leave pay is payable to the person". The hourly national
-- minimum wage is set by the Fair Work Commission and is an INPUT.
@export How much parental leave pay do I get for a day (s 65(2))?
GIVEN `hourly national minimum wage` IS A NUMBER @desc The national minimum wage per hour in operation on the day
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How much do I get for a day` MEANS
    `hourly national minimum wage` TIMES 76 DIVIDED BY 10

@export How much is my instalment (s 65(1))?
GIVEN `hourly national minimum wage` IS A NUMBER @desc The national minimum wage per hour (assumed the same on each day)
      `paid days in the instalment period` IS A NUMBER @desc The flexible PPL days in the instalment period for which you are paid
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How much is my instalment` MEANS
    `paid days in the instalment period` TIMES `How much do I get for a day` `hourly national minimum wage`

§§ `ss 71A, 101 -- will my employer pay me`

-- s 71A: a continuous flexible period needs a run of days that "(b) ... only consists of consecutive flexible PPL days for the
-- child that are week days; and (c) ... consists of at least 40 consecutive flexible PPL days for the child that are week days";
-- it "ends on the earlier of ... (i) the last day in the relevant period; (ii) the day before the child's first birthday". A run
-- that starts on or after the first birthday therefore cannot be one (an inference from (e)(ii)).
@export Can my run of days be a continuous flexible period (s 71A)?
GIVEN `born on` IS A NUMBER @desc The day your child was born, as YYYYMMDD
      `the run starts on` IS A NUMBER @desc The first day of the run, as YYYYMMDD
      `consecutive week days in the run` IS A NUMBER @desc How many consecutive week days the run has
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can my run be a continuous flexible period` IF
        `consecutive week days in the run` AT LEAST 40
    AND `the run starts on` LESS THAN `born on` PLUS 10000

-- s 101(1): the Secretary "must make a determination ... that a person's employer is to pay the person instalments" if satisfied
-- that "(a)" a payability or initial eligibility determination is in force; "(b) instalments are likely ... to be payable by the
-- employer to the person for at least 40 consecutive flexible PPL days that are week days; and (c) the person has, or will have,
-- been employed by the employer for at least 12 months immediately before" the expected date of birth (or, for a claim after the
-- birth, the later of that and the birth); "(d) the person has a continuous flexible period for the child and is likely to be an
-- Australian-based employee"; "(da) there are no other flexible PPL days prior to the person's continuous flexible period" paid or
-- initially eligible; "(e) the employer has an ABN". (2): "Paragraphs (1)(b) and (c) do not apply" if the employer "has made an
-- election under section 109 that applies to the person" and the person "has consented in the claim". (3A): not if the person "is
-- receiving an income support payment". (4): the Secretary "may decide not to" (period ended, special claimant, child died,
-- another claimant's debt, employer not fit and proper) -- asked as a fact. (1)(f), more than one employer, is not modelled.
DECLARE `My employment` HAS
    `a payability or initial eligibility determination is in force for me` IS A BOOLEAN
    `consecutive week days my employer would likely pay` IS A NUMBER
    `months I will have worked for my employer before the reference day` IS A NUMBER
    `I have a continuous flexible period and will be an Australian-based employee` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I have earlier flexible PPL days paid or initially eligible` IS A BOOLEAN
    `my employer has an ABN` IS A BOOLEAN
    `my employer elected under s 109 and I consented in my claim` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I am receiving an income support payment` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Secretary has decided under s 101(4) not to make one` IS A BOOLEAN

@export Will my employer pay me my parental leave pay (s 101)?
GIVEN `job` IS A `My employment` @desc Your employment and claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Will my employer pay me` IF
        `job`'s `a payability or initial eligibility determination is in force for me`
    AND (    `job`'s `my employer elected under s 109 and I consented in my claim`
         OR  (    `job`'s `consecutive week days my employer would likely pay` AT LEAST 40
              AND `job`'s `months I will have worked for my employer before the reference day` AT LEAST 12))
    AND `job`'s `I have a continuous flexible period and will be an Australian-based employee`
    AND (NOT (`job`'s `I have earlier flexible PPL days paid or initially eligible`))
    AND `job`'s `my employer has an ABN`
    AND (NOT (`job`'s `I am receiving an income support payment`))
    AND (NOT (`job`'s `the Secretary has decided under s 101(4) not to make one`))

§§ `ss 70, 72, 73, 74, 80, 84, 99 -- who pays me, and what my employer must do`

-- s 72(1A): the employer pays only "to the extent that the instalment is payable in relation to a flexible PPL day for the child
-- that falls within the continuous flexible period mentioned in the employer notice". s 84(2): "The Secretary must pay an
-- instalment that is payable to a person if the Secretary ... never made an employer determination"; (2A): and for a day "that
-- does not fall within the person's continuous flexible period". (ss 84(3)-(5), review, revocation and referral, are not
-- modelled.)
DECLARE `Who pays me` IS ONE OF
    `my employer`
    `the Secretary`

@export Who pays me for the day (ss 72(1A), 84(2), (2A))?
GIVEN `an employer determination is in force for me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Secretary has made an employer determination for you and your employer
      `the day is in my continuous flexible period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the day is in the continuous flexible period in the employer notice
GIVETH A `Who pays me`
`Who pays me for the day` MEANS
    IF `an employer determination is in force for me` AND `the day is in my continuous flexible period`
    THEN `my employer`
    ELSE `the Secretary`

-- s 73: "An employer has been paid enough to fund an instalment ... if the total of the PPL funding amounts paid to the employer
-- for the person for a child before that day is at least the total of ... (a) the amount of the instalments the employer has
-- previously paid ...; (b) the amount of the instalment; (c) the amount of any other instalment that is to be paid ... on the
-- payday".
@export Has my employer been paid enough to fund my instalment (s 73)?
GIVEN `funding my employer has received for me` IS A NUMBER @desc PPL funding amounts paid to your employer for you for the child
      `instalments my employer has already paid me` IS A NUMBER @desc Instalments your employer has already paid you for the child
      `this instalment` IS A NUMBER @desc The amount of this instalment
      `other instalments due on the same payday` IS A NUMBER @desc Any other instalment due to you on the same payday
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Has my employer been paid enough` IF
    `funding my employer has received for me` AT LEAST `instalments my employer has already paid me` PLUS `this instalment` PLUS `other instalments due on the same payday`

-- s 72(1): "An employer must pay an instalment to a person on the payday for the instalment if: (a) the instalment is payable to
-- the person; and (b) an employer determination is in force for the employer and the person on a day during the instalment period
-- ...; and (c) as at the payroll cut-off for the instalment, the employer has been paid enough to fund the instalment." (1A): only
-- for days in the continuous flexible period. s 64(2): the payday is the day the person "would usually be paid" for work.
@export Must my employer pay me the instalment on my usual payday (s 72(1), (1A))?
GIVEN `the instalment is payable to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether parental leave pay is payable to you for days in the instalment period
      `an employer determination is in force for me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether an employer determination is in force on a day in the period
      `my employer was paid enough by the payroll cut-off` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether s 73 is met at the payroll cut-off
      `the days are in my continuous flexible period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the days fall in the continuous flexible period in the employer notice
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must my employer pay me on my payday` IF
        `the instalment is payable to me`
    AND `an employer determination is in force for me`
    AND `my employer was paid enough by the payroll cut-off`
    AND `the days are in my continuous flexible period`

-- s 74: "must be paid in money by one, or a combination, of the following methods: (a) cash; (b) cheque, money order, postal order
-- or similar order, payable to the person; (c) the use of an electronic funds transfer system to credit an account held by the
-- person." (A civil penalty provision.)
DECLARE `How my employer pays me` IS ONE OF
    `cash`
    `a cheque or money order payable to me`
    `electronic transfer to my account`
    `a set-off against a debt I owe my employer`
    `shares or other non-money benefits`

@export Is this a way my employer may pay me my parental leave pay (s 74)?
GIVEN `the method` IS A `How my employer pays me` @desc How your employer pays the instalment
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May my employer pay me this way` IF
    CONSIDER `the method`
    WHEN `a set-off against a debt I owe my employer` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `shares or other non-money benefits` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

-- s 70(1): "An amount must not be deducted from an instalment except in accordance with section 67, 68, 69, 69A or 69B"; (2): "An
-- employer must comply with subsection (1)." What an employer may deduct: s 67(1) a deduction "(a) authorised by the person; and
-- (b) principally for the person's benefit" (s 67(3): "in writing" and specifying the amount); s 68 PAYG withholding the employer
-- "is required to withhold"; s 69(1) child support the employer "is required to deduct". ss 67(2), 69(2), 69A and 69B are
-- deductions by the Secretary only.
DECLARE `What my employer wants to deduct` IS ONE OF
    `an amount I authorised in writing, principally for my benefit`
    `PAYG withholding my employer is required to withhold`
    `child support my employer is required to deduct`
    `an overpayment of income support`
    `a debt I owe the Commonwealth`
    `a debt I owe my employer`

@export May my employer deduct this from my parental leave pay (ss 67-70)?
GIVEN `the deduction` IS A `What my employer wants to deduct` @desc What the deduction is for
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May my employer deduct it` IF
    CONSIDER `the deduction`
    WHEN `an amount I authorised in writing, principally for my benefit` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `PAYG withholding my employer is required to withhold` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `child support my employer is required to deduct` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- s 80: "An employer must, before the end of the next working day after paying an instalment to a person, give the person the
-- information prescribed by the PPL rules" (PPL rules s 32 says what; not modelled).
@export By the end of how many working days after paying me must my employer give me a record of payment (s 80)?
GIVEN `I was paid by my employer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your employer paid the instalment
GIVETH A NUMBER
`By how many working days must my employer give me a record` MEANS
    IF `I was paid by my employer` THEN 1 ELSE 0

-- s 99: "a period of unpaid leave is not to be taken to be a period of paid leave just because a person receives instalments of
-- parental leave pay for all or part of that period."
@export Does my unpaid leave count as paid leave because I get parental leave pay (s 99)?
GIVEN `I get parental leave pay during my unpaid leave` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you receive instalments during a period of unpaid leave
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does my unpaid leave become paid leave` IF
    `I get parental leave pay during my unpaid leave` AND FALSE

§§ `ss 115B, 115C -- superannuation on my parental leave pay`

-- s 115B(1): a PPL superannuation contribution "is payable ... for a person for an income year if either or both of the following
-- apply: (a) a PPL funding amount relating to the person is paid under section 75 in the income year by the Secretary to an
-- employer of the person; (b) an instalment is both: (i) payable to the person under section 63; and (ii) paid under section 84
-- in the income year by the Secretary to the person."
@export Will a PPL superannuation contribution be paid for me for the income year (s 115B)?
GIVEN `the Secretary paid my employer funding for me in the year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a PPL funding amount for you was paid to your employer in the income year
      `the Secretary paid me an instalment in the year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Secretary paid you an instalment directly in the income year
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Will a superannuation contribution be paid for me` IF
    `the Secretary paid my employer funding for me in the year` OR `the Secretary paid me an instalment in the year`

-- s 115C(1): the contribution is "(a) the base contribution for the person for the year multiplied by the SG charge percentage for
-- that year; (b) the nominal interest rate amount". (2): the base contribution is the PPL funding amounts paid to the employer and
-- the instalments paid by the Secretary in the income year. (4): "The SG charge percentage for an income year means the charge
-- percentage (within the meaning of subsection 17A(2) of the Superannuation Guarantee (Administration) Act 1992) divided by 100"
-- (the charge percentage is an INPUT). (5): the nominal interest rate amount is "the amount ... referred to in paragraph (1)(a)
-- multiplied by the amount worked out in accordance with the method prescribed by the PPL rules". PPL rules s 36: "Step 1.
-- Calculate the number of days (elapsed days)" from the first payment in the year to the Commissioner's s 115D determination;
-- "Step 2. Divide the number of elapsed days by 365. Step 3. Multiply the amount worked out at step 2 by 10% (rounded to 4 decimal
-- places and rounding up if the fifth decimal place is 5 or more)."
@export What is the multiplier for the nominal interest on my superannuation contribution (PPL rules s 36)?
GIVEN `elapsed days` IS A NUMBER @desc Days from the first PPL payment in the income year to the Commissioner's determination
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What is my nominal interest multiplier` MEANS
    TRUNC (`elapsed days` DIVIDED BY 365 TIMES 0.1 PLUS 0.00005) 4

@export How much PPL superannuation contribution is paid for me (s 115C)?
GIVEN `base contribution` IS A NUMBER @desc PPL funding amounts paid to your employer plus instalments the Secretary paid you, in the income year
      `charge percentage` IS A NUMBER @desc The charge percentage under SGAA s 17A(2) for the year (for example 12)
      `elapsed days` IS A NUMBER @desc Days from the first PPL payment in the income year to the Commissioner's determination
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How much superannuation contribution is paid for me` MEANS
    `the contribution before interest` PLUS `the contribution before interest` TIMES `What is my nominal interest multiplier` `elapsed days`
    WHERE
        `the contribution before interest` MEANS `base contribution` TIMES `charge percentage` DIVIDED BY 100
